Ubuntu security data
====================

zond's release builds include `ubuntu.bin`, a filtered and converted copy of
Canonical's Ubuntu security data: for the source packages zond can identify
on the network, which package version fixed each vulnerability in each
Ubuntu release, and which releases a vulnerability never affected.

It is derived from the Ubuntu Security Notices data,
Copyright Canonical Ltd., https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices,
published at https://security-metadata.canonical.com/ (the OSV and OpenVEX
archives), and licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International License,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.

The converted copy is licensed under the same terms. It is data read by the
program and not part of the program's source code, which is licensed under
the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later.

`zond update` fetches the current data from Canonical, and a scan uses
whichever of the two is newer.
